//
// Compile-time coverage scope of the DTP bench on Verilator, passed to the
// compiler from [coverage.verilator].build_args in dtp_sim_cfg.toml, so what it
// drops never enters the database. It approximates the instance scope of
// ../vcs/dtp_cov_scope.hier by source file: the line, branch and expression
// families grade the DUT's sources, the vendored cells included, and the
// bench, the coverage modules and the simulation-only modules leave them.
//
// `coverage_off` takes `-file` with globs only, so the scope is by source file,
// not by instance. The pattern is matched against the path as the compiler
// opened the file, so it starts with `*` and no `/` follows that `*` directly.

`verilator_config

// The bench: tb_top, its TB interfaces, its protocol checkers and the
// observation module it binds into every JTAG2AXI bridge.
coverage_off -file "*hw/sys/dtp/dv/tb/*"

// The shared VIP interfaces and protocol checkers and the open-drain wire
// model the bench instantiates.
coverage_off -file "*hw/common/dv/*"

// The functional-coverage modules. `coverage_off` leaves their `cover
// property` points, the `user` family, in the database.
coverage_off -file "*hw/sys/dtp/dv/cov/sv/*"

// The CDC jitter model the synchronizer primitives instantiate only under
// SIMULATION.
coverage_off -file "*prim_cdc_rand_delay.sv"
